<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!--
      OAuth callback for the PARENT app only.

      WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL, rather than adding the filter to the main
      manifest: `main/` is merged into BOTH flavors, so an intent-filter placed
      there would also be claimed by ParentVeda+ (the doctor build, which
      installs alongside via the `.doctor` applicationId suffix). Two installed
      apps advertising the same scheme means Android cannot tell which one asked
      — it shows the user a "Complete action using…" chooser in the middle of
      signing in, and picking wrong drops the session on the floor. Flavor
      source sets are Gradle's answer to exactly this: `src/parent/` merges only
      into the parent build. The doctor app signs in with email + password and
      needs no callback.

      This is only used by the BROWSER-REDIRECT providers (Facebook now, Apple
      later). Google's native flow never leaves the app and needs nothing here.

      The path back:
        Custom Tab → facebook.com → Supabase /auth/v1/callback
                   → com.parentveda.app://login-callback/  → this filter → app

      supabase_flutter listens for the incoming link itself and completes the
      session, which is what fires the `signedIn` event SocialAuth waits on.

      NOTE: `android:exported="true"` is required — the whole point is that an
      external app (the browser) can start this activity. And the scheme must
      match AuthConfig.oauthRedirectScheme exactly, in both spelling and case;
      Android does not normalise it, so a capital letter here silently means the
      redirect is never delivered.
    -->
    <application>
        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.BROWSABLE" />
                <data android:scheme="com.parentveda.app"
                      android:host="login-callback" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
